    // Winter wind: each month's factor is the cube of the monthly mean wind
    // speed at 10 m (the power-density relation) averaged over Moscow,
    // Novosibirsk and Anapa (Weather Spark, "Climate and Average Weather Year
    // Round in Russia", table "Average Wind Speed in Russia", read
    // 2026-10-25: Moscow 11.9, 11.7, 10.8, 9.8, 9.3, 8.6, 8.0, 8.5, 9.5, 10.5,
    // 11.0 and 11.7 mph; Novosibirsk 12.2, 12.0, 12.0, 11.6, 10.6, 8.7, 7.8,
    // 8.4, 9.7, 11.2, 12.2 and 12.7; Anapa 13.5, 13.7, 12.6, 10.6, 9.2, 9.0,
    // 9.6, 10.1, 10.6, 11.7, 12.8 and 13.4), over its year mean, times the
    // Eastern Interconnection's annual mean factor, 0.567 (authoring scale,
    // as in the other Plan 7 files; the cube law is an authoring judgment).
    // It peaks from November to February.
    wind: (monthly: [0.85, 0.84, 0.71, 0.52, 0.39, 0.29, 0.26, 0.31, 0.42, 0.6, 0.75, 0.86], persistence: 0.995, innovation_sd: 0.015, initial_sd: 0.15, band: 0.25),
    // Unit sizes and operating parameters follow the North American catalog
    // (spec section 3.2), except where a row names a local unit: coal is a
    // 230 MW unit, as at Kharanorskaya [P7-IPS-004], so its start-up cost
    // and ramp are scaled per MW (ruling 24). The CCGT row's project mixes a
    // 235 MW and two 160 MW units [P7-IPS-006] (Kommersant, read 2026-10-25),
    // so no single local CCGT size is sourced and the catalog keeps 500 MW.
    // Money and build months come from the Plan 7 research note by its
    // pacing method (ratios from its pacing table, at full precision; game
    // values rounded to 3 significant figures per kW, per kW-year or per
    // MWh, then multiplied by capacity; monthly fixed O&M is the
    // per-kW-year value x kW / 12, to the nearest rouble). The note has no
    // IPS/UPS fixed O&M row, so every kind's fixed O&M follows ruling 4
    // (authoring judgment: derived from its capital row by NA kind
    // relativity). The nuclear and hydro capital rows are the General
    // Scheme's investment over planned additions, which include VAT and
    // forecast prices of each year. Gas is the regulated FAS wholesale price
    // [P7-IPS-011], priced on its 7,900 kcal/m3 basis (33.080 GJ per 1,000
    // m3) and applied to the S&L heat rates without a calorific-basis
    // conversion (pacing judgment: the note has no conversion row), and fuel
    // only: the local marginal has no variable O&M row. Coal and nuclear
    // have no fuel row, so they follow ruling 19 (authoring judgment: no
    // sourced local fuel row): the North American game marginal x the local
    // reference tariff over the NA one, 5,803.835 / 100 = 58.03835, a
    // price-level proxy from [P7-IPS-001]. Start-ups follow ruling 2 (NA
    // start-up x local marginal / NA marginal, at full precision).
    catalog: [
        // Wind [P7-IPS-007] [P7-US-001]: IRENA's 2025 Russian market average,
        // 1,818 USD/kW x 83.6525 RUB/USD [P7-FX-023] = 152,080.2 RUB/kW x
        // (1,000 / 1,489 = 0.67159) = 102,135.8, so 102,000 RUB/kW x 300,000
        // kW = 30,600,000,000 (P7-IPS-008, a 2019 bid, is dated and a
        // cross-check only). Fixed O&M (ruling 4, authoring judgment: derived
        // from [P7-IPS-007] by NA kind relativity): 102,135.83 x NA fixed O&M
        // / capital (20.0 / 1,000 = 0.02) = 2,042.7, so 2,040 x 300,000 / 12
        // = 51,000,000. Build 3 months (ruling 1, authoring judgment: no
        // sourced local duration).
        (kind: Wind, capacity_mw: 300.0, min_stable: 0.0, ramp_mw_per_min: 0.0, startup_hours: 0.0, startup_cost: 0, marginal_cost_per_mwh: 0.0, fixed_om_per_month: 51000000, capital_cost: 30600000000, build_months: 3, capacity_credit: 0.2, book_life_months: 300, siting: Anywhere),
        // Nuclear (Kalinin, Smolensk, Novovoronezh and Leningrad are VVER and
        // RBMK stations of the first zone). Capital [P7-IPS-002] [P7-US-004]:
        // the General Scheme's 13,785e9 RUB for 29.299 million kW, incl. VAT
